# Todo.md Protocol

## Before Starting Any Work

1. **Read `todo.md` first** - understand current state, in-progress work, pitfalls, and rules
2. Check the "In Progress" section for active work
3. Review "Pitfalls" before making changes that could trigger known issues

## Before Every PR

1. **Update `todo.md` last** - after all other changes are complete
2. Move completed items to "Recently Done" (keep ~10 max)
3. Overflow from "Recently Done" goes to "History" section
4. Add new pitfalls discovered during work
5. Update "In Progress" section as needed

## Critical Rule

**Nothing in todo.md is ever deleted, only moved to History.**

- Completed items: Recently Done (max ~10) then History
- Outdated info: Move to History with date note
- Superseded decisions: Move to History

## Enforcement

A GitHub Actions workflow fails PRs that change code files but not `todo.md`.
- Label a PR `no-todo` to skip this check (e.g., docs-only changes)
- The workflow auto-passes for docs-only PRs

## File Location

`todo.md` lives at the repository root. A new agent can resume from this file alone.
